WEBVTT

00:14.600 --> 00:17.750
What is this?! It hurts!

00:18.350 --> 00:19.880
You're not going to finish him?

00:20.510 --> 00:23.489
If he could die, he'd be dead by now.

00:23.490 --> 00:24.879
What did you do to me?!

00:24.880 --> 00:28.769
Theoretically, that spell remains
active until the target dies.

00:28.770 --> 00:32.880
I used the power of Persephone's
curse to modify Prismatic Missile.

00:33.510 --> 00:36.770
Yuke! Aren't we friends?

00:37.050 --> 00:39.770
Yuke! Yuke!

00:52.470 --> 00:58.030
(I Left My A-Rank Party to Help My Former
Students Reach the Dungeon Depths)

02:13.490 --> 02:15.259
(One Week Later)

02:15.260 --> 02:16.239
(One Week Later)
So on that note...

02:16.240 --> 02:16.949
(Episode 9: A Six-Leaf Clover)

02:16.950 --> 02:20.999
(Episode 9: A Six-Leaf Clover)
I'd like to formally invite Nene to join Clover.

02:21.000 --> 02:22.379
(Episode 9: A Six-Leaf Clover)
Really? I'm glad to hear it.

02:22.380 --> 02:23.150
Really? I'm glad to hear it.

02:23.610 --> 02:26.000
Do you think she'll be able to get by?

02:26.430 --> 02:28.669
She's already doing very well.

02:28.670 --> 02:31.379
I almost forgot she was only
with us on a temporary basis.

02:31.380 --> 02:34.429
Then I have no objections.

02:34.430 --> 02:36.639
I'll take care of the paperwork, okay?

02:36.640 --> 02:38.839
Shouldn't we check with Nene first?

02:38.840 --> 02:39.640
Don't be silly!

02:40.200 --> 02:42.750
Do you think Nene would turn you down?

02:45.610 --> 02:49.030
I see you haven't quite mastered
concealing your presence yet.

02:49.400 --> 02:51.019
Um, well, you see...

02:51.020 --> 02:54.410
Silk wanted me to pass
along a message to Yuke...

02:54.700 --> 02:56.939
Eavesdropping is rude.

02:56.940 --> 02:58.410
I'm sorry!

02:58.820 --> 03:02.919
If you heard us, could you
give us your answer now, Nene?

03:02.920 --> 03:06.599
I-I was thinking of asking
you to let me join!

03:06.600 --> 03:09.459
But I didn't want to cause any trouble...

03:09.460 --> 03:11.930
It's no trouble. I'm happy to have you, Nene.

03:12.670 --> 03:14.019
We'll continue to count on you.

03:14.020 --> 03:14.800
Sure!

03:15.110 --> 03:18.269
Nene, try not to cause trouble
for any of them, okay?

03:18.270 --> 03:21.430
Of course! I'll dedicate my whole
heart to being useful to them!

03:23.080 --> 03:24.599
Master?

03:24.600 --> 03:28.940
It'll be a bit lonely without you...
but I'm also relieved.

03:29.270 --> 03:32.450
I hope you'll do your best with Yuke
and his companions from now on.

03:33.180 --> 03:34.199
I will.

03:34.200 --> 03:37.700
Well, then, I suppose the
rest is up to your leader.

03:39.260 --> 03:40.950
I'll be taking Nene.

03:44.030 --> 03:45.999
So what was the message?

03:46.000 --> 03:46.460
Oh!

03:46.740 --> 03:47.960
Here it is!

03:48.250 --> 03:50.710
She said you'd understand when you saw it.

03:52.920 --> 03:53.840
I see.

03:54.530 --> 03:55.840
What is it?

03:56.160 --> 03:59.029
Why don't we go pay Jamie a visit?

03:59.030 --> 03:59.990
Okay...

04:03.630 --> 04:06.600
Books, return to where you belong.

04:09.020 --> 04:10.610
Arrange Order!

04:16.860 --> 04:17.869
You're here?

04:17.870 --> 04:20.120
Efficient as ever, aren't you, Jamie?

04:20.540 --> 04:22.829
Oh, this is nothing.

04:22.830 --> 04:26.250
I wonder how long this place
was left abandoned, though.

04:26.650 --> 04:29.079
Benwood used to use this room.

04:29.080 --> 04:31.630
It ended up beyond his
control, so he just left it.

04:32.020 --> 04:35.429
With all these texts just
thrown in here at random,

04:35.430 --> 04:38.339
it'll take at least a
week to organize it all.

04:38.340 --> 04:39.390
A week?

04:40.050 --> 04:41.889
I'm actually working hard at this.

04:41.890 --> 04:43.179
I didn't mean that!

04:43.180 --> 04:47.569
I bet it'd take me half a year...
no, a full year to do all that!

04:47.570 --> 04:50.900
And you can do it in a week? So much respect!

04:51.180 --> 04:52.279
What she said.

04:52.280 --> 04:54.270
R-Really?

04:54.860 --> 04:56.819
Oh, right, Yuke...

04:56.820 --> 05:00.319
Um... I haven't thanked you yet, have I?

05:00.320 --> 05:01.660
Thank me? For what?

05:02.300 --> 05:06.160
You asked the guild master to let
me work at the guild, right?

05:06.550 --> 05:08.920
I didn't do anything at all.

05:09.360 --> 05:10.220
I see.

05:10.710 --> 05:14.939
Still, thanks. It's a huge
help having some real income.

05:14.940 --> 05:16.550
And there's Tec's medicine, too.

05:17.010 --> 05:19.049
Is your brother doing okay?

05:19.050 --> 05:22.859
Thanks to you. Your medicines
still work best of all.

05:22.860 --> 05:23.560
Thank you!

05:25.130 --> 05:26.769
Anyway, did you need something?

05:26.770 --> 05:28.489
Huh? Oh...

05:28.490 --> 05:30.519
Silk said she has business with you,

05:30.520 --> 05:33.379
so she'd like you to stop by
our base on your way home.

05:33.380 --> 05:34.820
Sure, but what for?

05:35.080 --> 05:36.989
I don't know, either.

05:36.990 --> 05:39.309
But you're almost done for the day, right?

05:39.310 --> 05:40.700
I mean, yeah...

05:42.650 --> 05:44.449
It's already winter, huh?

05:44.450 --> 05:46.950
It seems like it could
start snowing at any time.

05:47.820 --> 05:51.210
The nice thing about Finis is that
even when it snows, it doesn't stick.

05:51.730 --> 05:53.709
I can't stand snow.

05:53.710 --> 05:55.670
I like it when it's warm!

05:56.970 --> 05:59.889
The snow gets pretty deep where I'm from.

05:59.890 --> 06:02.170
I played in it all the
time when I was little.

06:05.920 --> 06:06.470
Ow!

06:08.480 --> 06:10.480
Take that!

06:14.000 --> 06:15.030
Hello?

06:15.730 --> 06:19.239
Oops, sorry. I got lost in thought.

06:19.240 --> 06:21.990
It's obvious what you're
thinking about, you know.

06:22.260 --> 06:23.199
Right?

06:23.200 --> 06:23.990
Yep.

06:25.130 --> 06:28.129
You realize you're probably making
the other girls worry, don't you?

06:28.130 --> 06:29.250
You're kidding...

06:30.300 --> 06:33.329
Being so easy to read is
just right for you, though.

06:33.330 --> 06:35.249
I bet you tend to get reckless.

06:35.250 --> 06:37.249
He totally does, Jamie!

06:37.250 --> 06:38.600
Oh, come on...

06:44.260 --> 06:47.270
Well, ladies first. Go on in.

06:47.580 --> 06:49.749
What the heck? That's not like you.

06:49.750 --> 06:52.109
Shouldn't you open the door for us, then?

06:52.110 --> 06:54.229
You're acting kinda weird, Yuke.

06:54.230 --> 06:55.150
Right?

06:57.230 --> 06:58.530
Pardon me...

07:02.660 --> 07:04.780
Surprise!

07:05.020 --> 07:05.319
Um... what?

07:05.320 --> 07:07.289
(Nene and Jamie, Welcome to Clover!)
Um... what?

07:07.290 --> 07:09.659
Th-That really did surprise me...

07:09.660 --> 07:11.910
Then the surprise was a success!

07:12.330 --> 07:14.880
I was afraid you'd figure us out.

07:15.470 --> 07:17.399
Yuke! You tricked me!

07:17.400 --> 07:19.800
I had to. Can you forgive me?

07:20.070 --> 07:22.829
Oh! That's why you sent me
with a message for Yuke!

07:22.830 --> 07:24.430
To get me outside!

07:24.760 --> 07:26.299
Exactly.

07:26.300 --> 07:27.680
I fell for it!

07:30.410 --> 07:33.690
I'm officially a member of Clover now?

07:34.320 --> 07:35.560
I'm so happy!

07:35.900 --> 07:37.959
It's a welcome party for both of you.

07:37.960 --> 07:39.409
So come on in.

07:39.410 --> 07:40.690
Don't mind if I do!

07:41.050 --> 07:42.979
No, I mean... I'm home!

07:42.980 --> 07:43.699
Welcome home!

07:43.700 --> 07:45.190
Welcome home.

07:45.720 --> 07:47.339
It wasn't too cold, was it?

07:47.340 --> 07:48.239
Nah!

07:48.240 --> 07:49.080
What is it?

07:50.280 --> 07:51.080
You didn't want this?

07:55.070 --> 07:58.119
I'm really happy... but...

07:58.120 --> 08:01.460
I caused so much trouble for you guys.

08:02.420 --> 08:04.530
Are you talking about Thunder Pike?

08:05.710 --> 08:08.859
Simon was an idiot,
Barry was an even bigger idiot,

08:08.860 --> 08:10.529
and Camilla looked down on me.

08:10.530 --> 08:13.629
And I'm just as scummy as them, of course.

08:13.630 --> 08:15.230
But it's fine now, isn't it?

08:15.600 --> 08:17.480
Because now you're here with us.

08:19.170 --> 08:23.950
You saved all of us that day, remember?

08:26.950 --> 08:29.699
That's right! We owe you our lives,

08:29.700 --> 08:31.450
and you're an expert we can count on!

08:31.760 --> 08:32.330
Yeah.

08:32.770 --> 08:34.769
You're already one of us.

08:34.770 --> 08:36.580
Let's go adventuring together!

08:42.370 --> 08:44.809
Jamie, you heard them.

08:44.810 --> 08:46.090
The topic's closed.

08:46.600 --> 08:51.100
We only need to begin our adventures
anew as Clover this time.

08:52.490 --> 08:54.340
Yeah. Thank you.

08:58.130 --> 09:00.549
What's wrong? This isn't like you.

09:00.550 --> 09:02.670
D-Don't tease me!

09:08.950 --> 09:12.450
Anyway, it's a welcome party! Let's go nuts!

09:16.110 --> 09:20.719
Now, in celebration of the formal
addition of Nene and Jamie to Clover...

09:20.720 --> 09:21.340
Che—

09:22.060 --> 09:22.840
What is it?

09:23.150 --> 09:25.779
There are six of us in Clover now...

09:25.780 --> 09:28.469
but are there six-leaf clovers?

09:28.470 --> 09:29.520
I don't know.

09:31.740 --> 09:35.219
There are. In the language of flowers,
they mean "glory" or "status."

09:35.220 --> 09:36.980
You're so smart, Jamie!

09:38.960 --> 09:41.140
"Glory," huh? That fits.

09:42.090 --> 09:45.190
Let's do our best to live
up to the "Clover" name!

09:45.920 --> 09:48.320
To the six-leaf Clover! Cheers!

09:48.680 --> 09:50.430
Cheers!

09:54.240 --> 09:56.779
Sorry you had to walk me home.

09:56.780 --> 09:59.960
I can't let a lady walk home alone at night.

10:00.220 --> 10:01.990
I swear, you're so...

10:02.730 --> 10:04.590
Nothing. Never mind.

10:05.740 --> 10:08.590
You know, back when I was starting out...

10:09.210 --> 10:11.840
I kind of admired you a little.

10:12.080 --> 10:12.690
Huh?

10:13.520 --> 10:15.639
You had a real city girl vibe.

10:15.640 --> 10:18.350
As a guy from the sticks,
I thought you seemed glamorous.

10:21.810 --> 10:24.180
Are you saying you don't think that anymore?

10:24.770 --> 10:25.989
Good question.

10:25.990 --> 10:28.360
I've lost a bit of my own innocence, too.

10:30.080 --> 10:32.740
You're definitely not as
cute as you used to be.

10:33.210 --> 10:35.399
C-Cute?!

10:35.400 --> 10:37.870
I mean... was it five years ago?

10:38.590 --> 10:41.339
Back when Thunder Pike first formed,

10:41.340 --> 10:44.079
you didn't even know how
to use running water,

10:44.080 --> 10:47.249
- and you were shocked to learn that
several stagecoaches ran every day.

10:47.250 --> 10:48.699
- Cobblestone...
- and you were shocked to learn that
several stagecoaches ran every day.

10:48.700 --> 10:52.260
You were even shocked by
the cobblestone roads.

10:52.750 --> 10:54.769
Was I that bad?

10:54.770 --> 10:58.350
Besides, wasn't it the same for Simon—

11:02.540 --> 11:04.650
Do you ever think back on those days?

11:07.100 --> 11:08.400
Sometimes, I guess.

11:09.010 --> 11:11.889
Our first quest was gathering
Morton herbs, wasn't it?

11:11.890 --> 11:12.910
That takes me back!

11:13.370 --> 11:17.259
Weren't Simon and Barry vehemently
opposed to it? That was rough.

11:17.260 --> 11:19.489
Yeah, they were.

11:19.490 --> 11:22.420
They kept grumbling that they'd
rather hunt a Vampire Goat.

11:22.780 --> 11:25.170
In the end, Mamar reasoned with them,

11:25.440 --> 11:28.170
and we settled on gathering medicinal herbs.

11:28.540 --> 11:33.680
Looking back on it, even back then,
you were oddly calm and knowledgeable.

11:34.140 --> 11:37.930
My uncle taught me everything there
is to know about adventuring.

11:39.230 --> 11:42.440
We did go on a lot of adventures.

11:43.140 --> 11:45.580
Though I don't have many happy
memories of those days...

11:46.450 --> 11:50.190
No, looking back now, I guess
there were lots of fun times.

11:51.750 --> 11:54.459
Once on shore, you pray no more, huh?

11:54.460 --> 11:56.269
That's a fair way to put it.

11:56.270 --> 11:59.950
I'm who I am now because of Thunder Pike.

12:01.430 --> 12:01.950
Yeah, but...

12:02.800 --> 12:06.460
Thunder Pike doesn't even exist anymore.

12:07.210 --> 12:09.960
Because I destroyed it.

12:12.560 --> 12:14.220
It's not your fault.

12:14.900 --> 12:16.840
That's just how things had to be.

12:17.830 --> 12:20.419
You grew more and more invisible,

12:20.420 --> 12:23.980
and the rest of us mistook
what you did for our own strength.

12:25.190 --> 12:28.730
I should've made an effort to
properly confront you guys.

12:29.170 --> 12:31.980
I think things would've fallen apart anyway.

12:32.500 --> 12:36.289
I can grasp your talents now
because of all we've been through,

12:36.290 --> 12:39.740
but back then, I don't think we
would've even listened to you.

12:40.140 --> 12:43.750
So I'll say it as many times as it takes.

12:44.320 --> 12:47.000
It definitely isn't your fault.

12:49.710 --> 12:51.250
It's ours.

12:52.540 --> 12:53.510
Jamie...

12:53.820 --> 12:56.260
So... let me start over.

12:58.030 --> 13:00.590
I don't know what I can really do,

13:01.190 --> 13:03.699
but in a year, when I can
return to adventuring,

13:03.700 --> 13:05.770
I'll work hard enough to
catch up to all of you.

13:06.280 --> 13:08.020
And I won't get it wrong next time.

13:09.030 --> 13:11.350
Jamie... I...

13:14.120 --> 13:17.160
We've been repaid more than enough already.

13:17.620 --> 13:20.780
So from now on, let's do our best as Clover.

13:22.860 --> 13:24.220
I swear...

13:24.860 --> 13:27.029
You haven't changed since the day we met.

13:27.030 --> 13:29.039
You're still a womanizer.

13:29.040 --> 13:31.709
No one's called me that before!

13:31.710 --> 13:34.710
I'm still a simple country boy,
I'll have you know!

13:41.550 --> 13:42.700
I'm back.

13:43.490 --> 13:44.310
Welcome home.

13:44.950 --> 13:46.369
You're alone?

13:46.370 --> 13:50.399
The others went with a wagon
to help move Nene's things.

13:50.400 --> 13:52.459
Huh? At this hour?

13:52.460 --> 13:57.049
She wants to be fully moved out of
Mamar's house by the end of the day.

13:57.050 --> 13:58.950
Tomorrow would've been just as good...

13:59.480 --> 14:03.439
I lost at rock-paper-scissors,
so I'm cleaning up.

14:03.440 --> 14:05.280
Got it. I'll help you.

14:05.820 --> 14:07.710
Okay. Thanks.

14:08.210 --> 14:09.080
Here.

14:09.340 --> 14:09.950
Yep.

14:11.880 --> 14:13.339
Here. Next.

14:13.340 --> 14:14.380
Oh, sure.

14:17.130 --> 14:18.590
Here. Next.

14:18.890 --> 14:19.560
Yep.

14:23.100 --> 14:26.029
This is... kind of fun.

14:26.030 --> 14:27.600
It's like we're newlyweds.

14:30.480 --> 14:32.350
S-Saved it...

14:33.380 --> 14:35.359
Was it that big a shock?

14:35.360 --> 14:37.110
No, I just...

14:40.050 --> 14:44.240
You don't want to see me
in an apron every day?

14:46.030 --> 14:46.740
I do.

14:52.250 --> 14:54.000
Your hands are cold.

14:55.180 --> 14:57.500
You're so unfair sometimes.

14:57.870 --> 15:01.010
So are you. You're always teasing me.

15:02.260 --> 15:05.880
You're still holding back
with me, aren't you?

15:06.650 --> 15:10.699
I know it's pathetic, but...
I don't know what I'm supposed to do.

15:10.700 --> 15:11.770
I'm confused.

15:12.160 --> 15:13.899
You're overthinking it.

15:13.900 --> 15:15.770
What do you want to do?

15:24.280 --> 15:25.410
Time's up.

15:28.860 --> 15:32.359
That's how I feel. You can
give me your answer later.

15:32.360 --> 15:33.929
R-Rain...

15:33.930 --> 15:35.419
We're back!

15:35.420 --> 15:36.669
Yuke, are you home?

15:36.670 --> 15:38.689
Help us carry this stuff!

15:38.690 --> 15:40.040
C-Coming!

15:43.180 --> 15:44.139
(One Month After Clover's Suspension Began)

15:44.140 --> 15:47.350
(One Month After Clover's Suspension Began)
So Clover gets to resume its activities tomorrow.

15:47.660 --> 15:50.129
Congratulations, Yuke.

15:50.130 --> 15:52.189
How was life under suspension?

15:52.190 --> 15:53.600
It was a nice break.

15:53.960 --> 15:55.569
I'm glad to hear that.

15:55.570 --> 15:59.109
So you've come here right off
the bat to accept a quest, then?

15:59.110 --> 16:02.610
No, I'm just here to say hello today...

16:03.490 --> 16:04.859
Do you have something?

16:04.860 --> 16:07.990
This information isn't public yet...

16:08.380 --> 16:11.120
but a new dungeon has been discovered.

16:11.690 --> 16:13.039
A new dungeon?

16:13.040 --> 16:16.819
It's been over ten years since a
new one was discovered, hasn't it?

16:16.820 --> 16:17.630
Where is it?

16:18.010 --> 16:21.260
On the bank of Lake Ryne,
near the trading city of Duna.

16:21.970 --> 16:25.010
Apparently, a local found
it while fishing there.

16:25.380 --> 16:31.279
Duna... Yeah, I've never heard
of any dungeons near there.

16:31.280 --> 16:34.270
Why not use it for Clover's comeback stream?

16:34.790 --> 16:37.539
Streaming the first look inside a new dungeon

16:37.540 --> 16:40.650
could definitely generate a lot of buzz...

16:41.180 --> 16:43.829
The Royal Academy is of the opinion that

16:43.830 --> 16:47.759
all the abnormalities that have
been occurring in various dungeons

16:47.760 --> 16:50.119
may have been aftereffects of
this new dungeon's appearance.

16:50.120 --> 16:53.160
So the dungeons were affecting each other?

16:53.560 --> 16:58.529
And since Clover did such an excellent
job investigating Achromatic Darkness,

16:58.530 --> 17:01.419
it was suggested that you investigate this one.

17:01.420 --> 17:02.250
Huh?

17:02.770 --> 17:05.419
And this request comes
from the kingdom, as well.

17:05.420 --> 17:08.930
A mission?! W-Well, that's a huge honor...

17:09.750 --> 17:13.019
But I feel like asking this of a
party that was just suspended

17:13.020 --> 17:15.430
kind of seems too good to be true.

17:15.740 --> 17:18.359
It was actually
the guild master who proposed it.

17:18.360 --> 17:21.190
That Benwood... Was he trying to surprise me?

17:21.490 --> 17:23.509
I'll talk it over with my party.

17:23.510 --> 17:26.969
I can't give an answer
on a quest this huge by myself.

17:26.970 --> 17:29.199
I'll be awaiting your favorable reply.

17:29.200 --> 17:31.510
Is Nene doing well?

17:32.380 --> 17:34.200
Yes. Do you miss her?

17:34.600 --> 17:39.019
Oh, Yuke. Please don't be so mean to me.

17:39.020 --> 17:40.709
It makes me want to return the favor.

17:40.710 --> 17:43.710
Um... Right.

17:48.570 --> 17:49.220
I'm back.

17:49.630 --> 17:51.220
Welcome home, Yuke.

17:52.400 --> 17:55.339
The look on your face says
you found us a good quest!

17:55.340 --> 17:57.589
Sort of... Wait, how can you tell?

17:57.590 --> 17:59.349
I can always tell with you, Yuke!

17:59.350 --> 18:02.829
R-Really? Where's everyone else?

18:02.830 --> 18:06.490
Silk's in her room, Rain's in the bath,
and Nene's shopping.

18:07.070 --> 18:09.329
I'll tell you all about it over dinner.

18:09.330 --> 18:12.239
We'll all decide together whether
or not to take the quest.

18:12.240 --> 18:16.629
Okay. I'm gonna go out to
the Adventurer's Guild for a bit, then.

18:16.630 --> 18:19.259
Jamie said she had something cool to lend me!

18:19.260 --> 18:20.000
"Cool"?

18:21.160 --> 18:22.750
You'll find out!

18:25.490 --> 18:27.260
Welcome home, Yuke.

18:28.510 --> 18:31.839
Thanks. Your hair's still wet.

18:31.840 --> 18:33.259
Do as you will.

18:33.260 --> 18:34.670
Okay, okay.

18:35.430 --> 18:38.270
The look on your face says
you found us a good quest.

18:40.160 --> 18:42.269
Marina said the same thing.

18:42.270 --> 18:44.759
If we're successful in this dungeon,

18:44.760 --> 18:47.530
will it lead us to another
chance at Achromatic Darkness?

18:47.840 --> 18:52.530
Maybe, but first, you gotta learn
to towel-dry your own hair.

18:52.880 --> 18:56.910
It's fine. I just want you to do this for me.

18:57.180 --> 18:58.400
Okay, okay.

18:58.910 --> 19:00.159
There, it's dry.

19:00.160 --> 19:01.989
Thanks, Yuke.

19:01.990 --> 19:04.419
I'm gonna go take a little nap.

19:04.420 --> 19:06.420
Don't catch a cold.

19:06.750 --> 19:08.920
You could come help me stay warm.

19:13.750 --> 19:14.740
Master.

19:15.680 --> 19:18.180
It must have been cold outside.

19:20.460 --> 19:24.219
The look on your face says
you found us a good quest.

19:24.220 --> 19:26.190
How can all of you tell?

19:26.870 --> 19:29.769
I was going to tell everyone
about it over dinner,

19:29.770 --> 19:32.309
but maybe I'll tell you first.

19:32.310 --> 19:34.759
Seems like a new dungeon's been discovered.

19:34.760 --> 19:35.570
Oh?

19:36.050 --> 19:38.679
We were asked to do the
first investigation on it.

19:38.680 --> 19:40.949
That should be a great experience.

19:40.950 --> 19:44.460
I suspect it'll make a great
stream for Clover, too.

19:46.160 --> 19:47.919
No, Mr. Feldio.

19:47.920 --> 19:48.459
Huh?

19:48.460 --> 19:51.869
I'll help you with the
preparations and planning,

19:51.870 --> 19:53.799
but you're our leader.

19:53.800 --> 19:56.469
Yeah, I know that, but...

19:56.470 --> 20:00.969
There can be no leader for our party but you.

20:00.970 --> 20:02.600
We'll continue to rely on you.

20:03.020 --> 20:04.349
Understood.

20:04.350 --> 20:08.389
Anyway, about the quest...
I didn't get the specifics.

20:08.390 --> 20:12.359
That look tells me you have every
intention of accepting it anyway.

20:12.360 --> 20:14.009
Figured me out, huh?

20:14.010 --> 20:17.660
Okay, I'll go back there right
now and get the details.

20:19.330 --> 20:24.109
When you have time, could you check to make
sure we have the supplies for a dungeon assault?

20:24.110 --> 20:25.120
Certainly.

20:25.500 --> 20:29.629
Oh, right! Please talk to Jamie
while you're at the guild.

20:29.630 --> 20:34.149
Huh? But even if we accept the
quest, we can't take Jamie.

20:34.150 --> 20:35.379
Not about that.

20:35.380 --> 20:37.089
We're having a party tonight!

20:37.090 --> 20:37.759
We are?

20:37.760 --> 20:40.510
To celebrate being released
from suspension.

20:41.080 --> 20:44.329
Please tell Jamie that she
and her brother are welcome.

20:44.330 --> 20:45.770
Got it. Thanks.

20:46.910 --> 20:47.770
Also...

20:48.440 --> 20:50.100
don't stop at just Rain.

20:50.700 --> 20:53.280
Please pamper me sometimes, too.

20:56.360 --> 20:57.529
I'm joking.

20:57.530 --> 20:58.929
Off you go!

20:58.930 --> 21:00.989
Uh, yeah, I'm going.

21:00.990 --> 21:02.509
I'm back!

21:02.510 --> 21:06.149
Hey, Yuke! The look on your face
says you found us a good quest!

21:06.150 --> 21:07.040
You, too?!

21:10.050 --> 21:13.550
A mission from the kingdom...
A new dungeon to conquer...

21:13.920 --> 21:18.159
There couldn't be a better
quest for Clover's comeback!

21:18.160 --> 21:20.710
All right! Let's have fun, but be careful!

22:55.940 --> 22:56.539
(Special Party Feature: Clover!)

22:56.540 --> 22:59.819
(Special Party Feature: Clover!)
Next time, "Special Party Feature: Clover!"

22:59.820 --> 23:00.950
(Special Party Feature: Clover!)
